{
  "entries": [
    {"source_ref": "note:1", "body": "Photosynthesis converts light energy into chemical energy in chloroplasts. The Calvin cycle fixes carbon dioxide."},
    {"source_ref": "note:2", "body": "Mitochondria produce ATP through cellular respiration. Glycolysis happens in the cytoplasm."},
    {"source_ref": "note:3", "body": "Enzymes lower activation energy. The substrate binds to the active site of the enzyme."},
    {"source_ref": "note:4", "body": "Osmosis moves water across a semipermeable membrane toward higher solute concentration."},
    {"source_ref": "note:5", "body": "Plate tectonics explains earthquakes and volcanic arcs at plate boundaries."},
    {"source_ref": "note:6", "body": "Mendel's pea experiments established dominant allele and recessive allele patterns."}
